  "content": "| Name:                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                     |\n| --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| \\[ \\[ [<'font-style'>](CSS-FONTS-4#propdef-font-style) [&#124;&#124;](CSS-VALUES-4#comb-any) [\\<font-variant-css2>](CSS-FONTS-4#font-variant-css21-values) &#124;&#124; [<'font-weight'>](CSS-FONTS-4#propdef-font-weight) &#124;&#124; [\\<font-width-css3>](CSS-FONTS-4#font-width-css3-values) \\][?](CSS-VALUES-4#mult-opt) [<'font-size'>](CSS-FONTS-4#propdef-font-size) \\[ / [<'line-height'>](CSS2#propdef-line-height) \\]? [<'font-family'>](CSS-FONTS-4#propdef-font-family)[#](CSS-VALUES-4#mult-comma) \\] [&#124;](CSS-VALUES-4#comb-one) [\\<system-font-family-name>](CSS-FONTS-4#system-font-family-name-value) |\n| see individual properties                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                 |\n| all elements and text                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                     |\n| yes                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                       |\n| see individual properties                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                 |\n| see individual properties                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                 |\n| per grammar                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                               |\n| see individual properties                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                 |\n\nTests\n\n*   [inheritance.html](https://wpt.fyi/results/css/css-fonts/inheritance.html) [(live test)](http://wpt.live/css/css-fonts/inheritance.html) [(source)](https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/blob/master/css/css-fonts/inheritance.html)\n*   [font-family-comma.html](https://wpt.fyi/results/css/css-fonts/font-family-comma.html) [(live test)](http://wpt.live/css/css-fonts/font-family-comma.html) [(source)](https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/blob/master/css/css-fonts/font-family-comma.html)\n*   [font-shorthand-serialization-001.html](https://wpt.fyi/results/css/css-fonts/font-shorthand-serialization-001.html) [(live test)](http://wpt.live/css/css-fonts/font-shorthand-serialization-001.html) [(source)](https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/blob/master/css/css-fonts/font-shorthand-serialization-001.html)\n*   [font-shorthand-serialization-font-stretch.html](https://wpt.fyi/results/css/css-fonts/font-shorthand-serialization-font-stretch.html) [(live test)](http://wpt.live/css/css-fonts/font-shorthand-serialization-font-stretch.html) [(source)](https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/blob/master/css/css-fonts/font-shorthand-serialization-font-stretch.html)\n*   [font-shorthand-serialization-prevention.html](https://wpt.fyi/results/css/css-fonts/font-shorthand-serialization-prevention.html) [(live test)](http://wpt.live/css/css-fonts/font-shorthand-serialization-prevention.html) [(source)](https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/blob/master/css/css-fonts/font-shorthand-serialization-prevention.html)\n*   [font-shorthand-subproperties-reset.html](https://wpt.fyi/results/css/css-fonts/font-shorthand-subproperties-reset.html) [(live test)](http://wpt.live/css/css-fonts/font-shorthand-subproperties-reset.html) [(source)](https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/blob/master/css/css-fonts/font-shorthand-subproperties-reset.html)\n*   [quoted-generic-ignored.html](https://wpt.fyi/results/css/css-fonts/quoted-generic-ignored.html) [(live test)](http://wpt.live/css/css-fonts/quoted-generic-ignored.html) [(source)](https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/blob/master/css/css-fonts/quoted-generic-ignored.html)\n*   [font-computed.html](https://wpt.fyi/results/css/css-fonts/parsing/font-computed.html) [(live test)](http://wpt.live/css/css-fonts/parsing/font-computed.html) [(source)](https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/blob/master/css/css-fonts/parsing/font-computed.html)\n*   [font-invalid.html](https://wpt.fyi/results/css/css-fonts/parsing/font-invalid.html) [(live test)](http://wpt.live/css/css-fonts/parsing/font-invalid.html) [(source)](https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/blob/master/css/css-fonts/parsing/font-invalid.html)\n*   [font-valid.html](https://wpt.fyi/results/css/css-fonts/parsing/font-valid.html) [(live test)](http://wpt.live/css/css-fonts/parsing/font-valid.html) [(source)](https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/blob/master/css/css-fonts/parsing/font-valid.html)\n*   [font-shorthand.html](https://wpt.fyi/results/css/css-fonts/variations/font-shorthand.html) [(live test)](http://wpt.live/css/css-fonts/variations/font-shorthand.html) [(source)](https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/blob/master/css/css-fonts/variations/font-shorthand.html)\n\nThe syntax of this property is based on a traditional typographical shorthand notation to set multiple properties related to fonts. For historical and backwards-compatibility reasons, it is *almost* a shorthand property.\n\nThe [font](CSS-FONTS-4#propdef-font) property is, except as described below, a shorthand property for setting [font-style](CSS-FONTS-4#propdef-font-style), [font-variant](CSS-FONTS-4#propdef-font-variant), [font-weight](CSS-FONTS-4#propdef-font-weight), [font-width](CSS-FONTS-4#propdef-font-width), [font-size](CSS-FONTS-4#propdef-font-size), [line-height](CSS2#propdef-line-height), [font-family](CSS-FONTS-4#propdef-font-family) at the same place in the stylesheet.\n\nValues for the [font-variant](CSS-FONTS-4#propdef-font-variant) property can also be included but only those supported in CSS 2.1; none of the font-variant values added in CSS Fonts Levels 3 or 4 can be used in the [font](CSS-FONTS-4#propdef-font) shorthand:\n\n```\n<font-variant-css2>\n    = normal | small-caps\n```\n\nValues for the [font-width](CSS-FONTS-4#propdef-font-width) property can also be included but only those supported in CSS Fonts level 3, none of the font-width values added in this specification can be used in the [font](CSS-FONTS-4#propdef-font) shorthand:\n\n```\n<font-width-css3>\n    = normal | ultra-condensed | extra-condensed | condensed |\n    semi-condensed | semi-expanded | expanded | extra-expanded |\n    ultra-expanded\n```\n\nTherefore we have the following classification of font-related properties and their interaction with the [font](CSS-FONTS-4#propdef-font) property:\n\nSet Explicitly \n\nThese longhand properties may also be set using the [font](CSS-FONTS-4#propdef-font) shorthand property:\n\n*   [font-family](CSS-FONTS-4#propdef-font-family)\n*   [font-size](CSS-FONTS-4#propdef-font-size)\n*   [font-width](CSS-FONTS-4#propdef-font-width)\n*   [font-stretch](CSS-FONTS-4#propdef-font-stretch) (css3)\n*   [font-style](CSS-FONTS-4#propdef-font-style)\n*   [font-variant-caps](CSS-FONTS-4#propdef-font-variant-caps) (css2)\n*   [font-weight](CSS-FONTS-4#propdef-font-weight)\n*   [line-height](CSS2#propdef-line-height)\n\nReset Implicitly \n\nThese properties are a [reset-only sub-property](CSS-CASCADE-5#reset-only-sub-property) of the [font](CSS-FONTS-4#propdef-font) property and thus may not be set, but are reset to their initial values:\n\n*   [font-feature-settings](CSS-FONTS-4#propdef-font-feature-settings)\n*   [font-kerning](CSS-FONTS-4#propdef-font-kerning)\n*   [font-language-override](CSS-FONTS-4#propdef-font-language-override)\n*   [font-optical-sizing](CSS-FONTS-4#propdef-font-optical-sizing)\n*   [font-size-adjust](CSS-FONTS-4#propdef-font-size-adjust)\n*   [font-variant-alternates](CSS-FONTS-4#propdef-font-variant-alternates)\n*   [font-variant-caps](CSS-FONTS-4#propdef-font-variant-caps) (css3 and above)\n*   [font-variant-east-asian](CSS-FONTS-4#propdef-font-variant-east-asian)\n*   [font-variant-emoji](CSS-FONTS-4#propdef-font-variant-emoji)\n*   [font-variant-ligatures](CSS-FONTS-4#propdef-font-variant-ligatures)\n*   [font-variant-numeric](CSS-FONTS-4#propdef-font-variant-numeric)\n*   [font-variant-position](CSS-FONTS-4#propdef-font-variant-position)\n*   [font-variation-settings](CSS-FONTS-4#propdef-font-variation-settings)\n\nCascaded Independently \n\nThese (despite the property name starting with \"font-\") are not [longhand properties](CSS-CASCADE-5#longhand) of the [font](CSS-FONTS-4#propdef-font) and thus are neither set nor reset by the font property:\n\n*   [font-palette](CSS-FONTS-4#propdef-font-palette)\n*   [font-synthesis-weight](CSS-FONTS-4#propdef-font-synthesis-weight)\n*   [font-synthesis-style](CSS-FONTS-4#propdef-font-synthesis-style)\n*   [font-synthesis-small-caps](CSS-FONTS-4#propdef-font-synthesis-small-caps)\n*   [font-synthesis-position](CSS-FONTS-4#propdef-font-synthesis-position)\n\nAll subproperties of the [font](CSS-FONTS-4#propdef-font) property in the Set Explicitly and Reset Implicitly groups are first reset to their initial values.\n\nThen, those properties the Set Explicitly group that are given explicit values in the [font](CSS-FONTS-4#propdef-font) shorthand are set to those values. For a definition of allowed and initial values, see the individual longhand property definitions.\n\n> **Example:** ```\n> p { font: 12pt/14pt sans-serif }\n> p { font: 80% sans-serif }\n> p { font: x-large/110% \"new century schoolbook\", serif }\n> p { font: bold italic large Palatino, serif }\n> p { font: normal small-caps 120%/120% fantasy }\n> p { font: condensed oblique 12pt \"Helvetica Neue\", serif; }\n> p { font: condensed oblique 25deg 753 12pt \"Helvetica Neue\", serif; }\n> ```\n>\n> In the second rule, the font size percentage value (\"80%\") refers to the computed [font-size](https://drafts.csswg.org/css-fonts-4#propdef-font-size) of the parent element. In the third rule, the line height percentage (\"110%\") refers to the font size of the element itself.\n>\n> The first three rules do not specify the [font-variant](https://drafts.csswg.org/css-fonts-4#propdef-font-variant) and [font-weight](https://drafts.csswg.org/css-fonts-4#propdef-font-weight) explicitly, so these properties receive their initial values ([normal](https://drafts.csswg.org/css-fonts-4#font-variant-normal-value)). Notice that the font family name \"new century schoolbook\", which contains spaces, is enclosed in quotes. The fourth rule sets the font-weight to [bold](https://drafts.csswg.org/css-fonts-4#valdef-font-weight-bold), the [font-style](https://drafts.csswg.org/css-fonts-4#propdef-font-style) to [italic](https://drafts.csswg.org/css-fonts-4#valdef-font-style-italic), and implicitly sets font-variant to normal.\n>\n> The fifth rule sets the [font-variant](https://drafts.csswg.org/css-fonts-4#propdef-font-variant) ([small-caps](https://drafts.csswg.org/css-fonts-4#valdef-font-variant-caps-small-caps)), the [font-size](https://drafts.csswg.org/css-fonts-4#propdef-font-size) (120% of the parent’s font size), the [line-height](https://drafts.csswg.org/css2/#propdef-line-height) (120% of the font size) and the [font-family](https://drafts.csswg.org/css-fonts-4#propdef-font-family) ([fantasy](https://drafts.csswg.org/css-fonts-4#valdef-font-family-fantasy)). It follows that the keyword normal applies to the two remaining properties: [font-style](https://drafts.csswg.org/css-fonts-4#propdef-font-style) and [font-weight](https://drafts.csswg.org/css-fonts-4#propdef-font-weight).\n>\n> The sixth rule sets the [font-style](https://drafts.csswg.org/css-fonts-4#propdef-font-style), [font-width](https://drafts.csswg.org/css-fonts-4#propdef-font-width), [font-size](https://drafts.csswg.org/css-fonts-4#propdef-font-size), and [font-family](https://drafts.csswg.org/css-fonts-4#propdef-font-family), the other font properties being set to their initial values.\n>\n> The seventh rule sets [font-style](https://drafts.csswg.org/css-fonts-4#propdef-font-style) to oblique 25deg, [font-weight](https://drafts.csswg.org/css-fonts-4#propdef-font-weight) to 753, and [font-width](https://drafts.csswg.org/css-fonts-4#propdef-font-width) to [condensed](https://drafts.csswg.org/css-fonts-4#valdef-font-width-condensed). Note that the 25deg in this rule must be immediately following the \"oblique\" keyword.\n\nSince the [font-width](CSS-FONTS-4#propdef-font-width) property was not defined in CSS 2.1, when using font-width values within [font](CSS-FONTS-4#propdef-font) rules, authors should include a extra version compatible with older user agents:\n\n```\np {\n  font: 80% sans-serif;   /* for older user agents */\n  font: condensed 80% sans-serif;\n}\n```\n\nSystem fonts can only be set as a whole; that is, the font family, size, weight, style, etc. are all set at the same time. These values can then be altered individually if desired. If no font with the indicated characteristics exists on a given platform, the user agent should either intelligently substitute (e.g., a smaller version of the [caption](CSS-FONTS-4#valdef-font-caption) font might be used for the [small-caption](CSS-FONTS-4#valdef-font-small-caption) font), or substitute a user agent default font. As for regular fonts, if, for a system font, any of the individual properties are not part of the operating system’s available user preferences, those properties should be set to their initial values.\n\nThat is why this property is \"almost\" a shorthand property: system fonts can only be specified with this property, not with [font-family](CSS-FONTS-4#propdef-font-family) itself, so [font](CSS-FONTS-4#propdef-font) allows authors to do more than the sum of its subproperties. However, the individual properties such as [font-weight](CSS-FONTS-4#propdef-font-weight) are still given values taken from the system font, which can be independently varied.\n\nNote that the keywords used for the system fonts listed above are only treated as keywords when they occur in the initial position, in other positions the same string is treated as part of the font family name:\n\n```\nfont: menu;        /* use the font settings for system menus */\nfont: large menu;  /* use a font family named \"menu\" */\n```\n\n> **Example:** ```\n> button { font: 300 italic 1.3em/1.7em \"FB Armada\", sans-serif }\n> button p { font: menu }\n> button p em { font-weight: bolder }\n> ```\n>\n> If the font used for dropdown menus on a particular system happened to be, for example, 9-point Charcoal, with a weight of 600, then P elements that were descendants of BUTTON would be displayed as if this rule were in effect:\n>\n> ```\n> button p { font: 600 9pt Charcoal }\n> ```\n>\n> Because the [font](https://drafts.csswg.org/css-fonts-4#propdef-font) shorthand resets to its initial value any property not explicitly given a value, this has the same effect as this declaration:\n>\n> ```\n> button p {\n>   font-style: normal;\n>   font-variant: normal;\n>   font-weight: 600;\n>   font-size: 9pt;\n>   line-height: normal;\n>   font-family: Charcoal\n> }\n> ```",
